    "probe_recall": 0.5121951219512195,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class it names. Every step runs inside one shared write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so all the reads and the final write commit once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without the `OWNER_ADMIN` role the request never enters the pipeline (403).\n\n## Validations and side-effects, in execution order\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 *validation.* Binds the request body (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 the one and only body binding). Rejects **400** (`OwnerFieldsMissingException`, listing each bad field) if `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank, or if `address` is blank *after normalization*. Republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n2. **`RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`** \u2014 *validation.* Only if `registrationDate` is supplied: rejects **400** (`OwnerRegistrationDateInvalidException`) if it is after the server's current date. Absent date is allowed.\n\n3. **`RequireOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 *validation.* Only if `postcode` is supplied: must be exactly 4 digits; and when the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range. Otherwise **400** (`OwnerPostcodeInvalidException`). Absent postcode allowed.\n\n4. **`NormalizeOwnerAddress`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Rewrites `address` in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Rewrites `telephone` in place to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+CC` or assume `+61` dropping one leading `0`). Must be 8\u201315 digits, with country-specific length (`+61`\u21929 national digits, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400** (`OwnerTelephoneInvalidException`).\n\n6. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Only if `email` present/non-blank: must match the email regex or **400** (`OwnerEmailInvalidException`); valid address is lower-cased in place.\n\n7. **`RequireNonDisposableOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *validation.* Only if email present: rejects **400** (`OwnerEmailDisposableException`) when the domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`.\n\n8. **`RequireOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 *validation.* Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50, rejects **409** (`OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`).\n\n9. **`RequireDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 *validation.* Computes the effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled off weekends) and counts existing owners already registered that day; if \u2265 100, rejects **429** (`OwnerDailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n10. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps the validated body to a new `Owner` and sets `registrationDate` to the effective business-day-adjusted date (defaults absent date to today; rolls Sat/Sun forward to Monday).\n\n11. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region derived from postcode/city, HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n12. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n\n13. **`RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 *validation.* Unless the request set `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects **409** (`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException`) if any existing owner already has the same `householdId`.\n\n14. **`RequireUniqueOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 *validation.* Rejects **409** (`OwnerIdentityDuplicateException`) if the whole derived identity key `telephone|email|householdId` exactly matches an existing owner's.\n\n15. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus one (or 1 when no householdId).\n\n16. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n17. **`AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of registration year).\n\n18. **`AssignMembershipLevel`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Computes `membershipPoints` (+2 email present, +1 namesakeCount==0, +2 householdSize\u22653, +3 tenure>365 days) and maps to `membershipLevel` 1\u20134. At creation tenure is 0, so a new owner never exceeds level 3.\n\n19. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` if strictly more than 80 owners already exist for that registration day.\n\n20. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Unless `sharesHousehold=true` (then flags cleared), sets `possibleDuplicate=true` / `possibleDuplicateOf=<lowest matching id>` when an existing owner shares last name (case-insensitive) and postcode; otherwise false/null.\n\n21. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n22. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Logs an `AUDIT` line: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n23. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The transaction commits here.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- The body is bound **once** (step 1); every later step reads the same published `OwnerFieldsDto`/`Owner` object and mutates it in place \u2014 the normalizations in steps 4\u20136 are what steps 8\u201320 and the stored record see.\n- Ordering is deliberate: field/format validations (400s) run before the duplicate/capacity checks (409/429), and all duplicate checks read the repository *before* `SaveOwner`, so counts exclude the owner being created.\n- Because everything shares one transaction, a throw in any step rolls the whole thing back \u2014 nothing is persisted unless step 21 is reached."
